& [LookupSurface]
  + LexicalAnchorLookupRequest binds one exact Slice4B1 index one exact catalogue one exact fabric tokenizer ordered original terms and finite caller budgets
  + lookup_lexical_anchors whole-validates the supplied index against the same admitted catalogue and SemanticFabric before using any posting
  + each original term retains its normalized token-occurrence account including duplicate terms repeated tokens and terms producing no eligible tokens
  + lookup forms the complete unique-token posting union before aggregation and refuses rather than returning a partial discovery when posting or match budget is exceeded
  + exact postings group only by complete SemanticAddress and retain token surface kind surface digest occurrence and source-evidence identities

& [OrderAndProof]
  + coverage basis points are floor of matched unique eligible tokens times ten-thousand divided by all unique eligible tokens
  + repeated terms repeated token occurrences aliases and surface multiplicity do not inflate coverage
  + matches sort by descending coverage then complete serialized SemanticAddress and equal-coverage ambiguity remains visible without winner selection
  + unmatched eligible tokens remain explicit and empty-token terms remain visible through their term account
  + lexical_anchor_lookup_proof_digest commits request catalogue fabric index tokenizer terms posting account matches evidence coverage unmatched set order and fixed non-authority statement under a distinct domain
  + validate_lexical_anchor_lookup_result first validates form then reruns the complete lookup and requires exact equality so a self-resealed mutation cannot authorize itself

& [ClosedCLI]
  + cantor-anchor-lab query accepts one explicit signed runtime-environment path and ordinary text
  + the CLI preflights and re-admits the environment then derives the catalogue lexical sidecar and lookup result entirely in memory
